# Visage of Dread // Dread Osseosaur. As the Visage enters, Bot2 reveals its hand and Bot1 chooses an artifact or creature
# card from it - not the Lightning Bolt (refused), the Ornithopter - which Bot2 discards. "Craft with two creatures
# {5}{B}" (CR 702.167a-b) needs two from among the creatures Bot1 controls and the creature cards in its graveyard: with
# only its bolted Ornithopter in the graveyard it is not offered on turn seven; once a second Ornithopter is on the
# battlefield it is, and one creature alone is no answer (refused) - the two, one from each zone (the craft rulings), are.
# Dread Osseosaur, a 5/4 black creature with menace, may mill two cards as it enters (accepted) and as it attacks
# (declined).

